
FAMECfgMonitor is a monitor tool which can be started everytime to monitor
the FAME Config feature. Exactly it displays every at the moment loaded
FAME Config data structure. With every data structure it also monitors
important informations like the opencounter, Read/Write (Modify) status,
the size of the data structure, the name/type of the data structure,
Num (fcr_ConfigNum) indicator, Num2 (fcr_ConfigNum2) indicator, 
String (fcr_ConfigStr) indicator and the path of the data file on disk.

You will see a listview where in every entry a loaded data structure 
will be displayed. Below the listview you will see the String (fcr_ConfigStr)
indicator and the path of the data file on disk in a longer version.
You will also see the name and description of the first owner of the
currently selected data strcuture. If the field below the listview displays 
nothing you first have to select an entry in the listview!

By clicking on the button "Owners" (if a entry in the listview is selected)
or by double clicking an entry in the listview a second window with a listview
will popup. In this window you will see all currently obtained owners
(sharing owners) of the currently selected data structure. You will see the
tool's names and their description if they have set one. Below you will
also see the name and description in a longer form, but only if you have
selected an owner. Button "Close" closes the owner window.

Back to the main window. Button "Remove" is disabled and not functionable
at the moment.. and i think this is good so. Button "Quit" to end
FAMECfgMonitor.


Ok some additional words. Most of you might know me enough ;) So be informed
that the usage of FAMECfgMonitor is very very easy. Just start it.
Both windows are running asynchron together and are not blocking each other.
So feel free to leave the second (Owners) window open. Both windows
automatical refresh if something changed and both windows are interacting.

This means if you display the "Owners" of a data structure and you now want
to display the "Owners" of a different one that you don't need to close and 
re-open the owner window. Just click on the data structure you want and
if the Owner window is open it automatically refreshes it with the "Owners"
of the new selected data structure. Also if something changes to the
"Owners" or the data structures like a new "Owner" has been added or removed
or the opencounter or the modify status has changed the windows will 
automatically update to the new information... well it's a monitor ;)

